  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1112 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nThe HRRR/RRFS suggest that highs will be back on the rise across \neastern OK on Friday, so temps were raised a touch above the model\nblend (NBM) there. Ensemble and deterministic data continues to\nindicate that the H5 ridge currently over the Southwest will \nbuild over the region this weekend, with the ridge center \neventually settling over the mid-Mississippi and Ohio Valleys next\nweek. Expect above average temps to continue. The latest data \nshows a tight gradient over the Plains over the weekend and into \nnext week, so hot, dry and breezy afternoons are ahead. This will \nnot help the ongoing drought situation, and fire weather concerns \nwill likely exist at least locally each afternoon. Ensemble data \nshows some signal for isolated storms in the terrain by Tuesday or\nWednesday, but coverage/confidence is certainly too low to \nmention and will not change the overall message.\n\nThe latest CPC outlook for week 2, which will include the Labor\nDay holiday weekend, suggests that warmer than average temps and\nbelow average precip is favored. No sign of fall is on the horizon\nyet.\n\nLacy",
